(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The C world of pyi's ctypes (queue 244; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 244\"; the user's 244-2 (a)): one ci"] [4 1 "// program per process over one address space, the node program go/arbace/clib/ctypestest (musl's libc and libm,"] [5 1 "// CPython's Modules/_ctypes/_ctypes_test.c, the glue's table of libc's functions), opened on _ctypes's first use. Every"] [6 1 "// ctypes buffer is memory of this program (malloc'd there), so an address ctypes gives is one C dereferences as is."] [7 1 "// Its names: the functions by the program's names, the data by the names the node program's static commands carry."] [8 1 "// The handles of 244-3 (a), the first part: a Python object passed to C as PyObject * (py_object) is the address of a"] [9 1 "// proxy in the world's memory holding the documented head (ob_refcnt, ob_type), one proxy per object."] [26 30 "// a data symbol's name -> its static's index"] [27 30 "// a data symbol's name -> its static's size (queue 475: _PyRuntime's layout checked)"] [32 1 "// cw is the world, opened on the first use."] [63 1 "// symbol is dlsym in the world: a function's address, else a data symbol's; 0 when the world has neither."] [72 2 "// a C API function the world does not reference (pythonapi's): a function of the program whose body is its native"] [79 2 "// a data symbol of the C API the world does not define (pythonapi's in_dll): made on its first lookup"] [83 1 "// pyData are the C API's data symbols made by pyDataSymbol, by name: their memory, kept for the process."] [86 1 "// pyDataSymbol is a data symbol of CPython's that pythonapi reads and the world's C does not reference (queue 261,"] [87 1 "// test_values): Py_OptimizeFlag (an int, sys.flags.optimize), and _PyImport_FrozenBootstrap, _PyImport_FrozenStdlib"] [88 1 "// and _PyImport_FrozenTest (Python/frozen.c's const struct _frozen *, each pointing to its table: name, code, size,"] [89 1 "// is_package, 24 bytes an entry, a zero entry last; the code is the frozen module's marshalled code object, its name"] [90 1 "// and code kept in the world). 0 for any other name, or when the data cannot be made."] [138 1 "// cbuf is a ctypes object's own memory: size bytes of the world's heap, zeroed, freed when the Go value it belongs to"] [139 1 "// is collected (the free queued on the library, run before its next call, as arbace/clib's Defer)."] [155 1 "// keepBytes is a copy of b in the world's memory with a terminating NUL (a bytes object passed as char *: CPython"] [156 1 "// hands C the object's own buffer; here its copy, kept alive by the ctypes object that holds it)."] [165 1 "// keepWide is s as a NUL-terminated wchar_t string (UTF-32, ci's wchar_t) in the world's memory."] [176 1 "// The keep object a setter returns (the ctypes object's b_objects holds it): a buffer kept alive."] [183 1 "// The handles' reference counts (queue 262; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 262\"): a proxy's ob_refcnt counts"] [184 1 "// the references C holds, Python's own references being Go's. A proxy is made with count 0 (a borrowed reference: an"] [185 1 "// argument, a container's item); a new reference C receives raises it (newRef), Py_DecRef lowers it. A proxy whose"] [186 1 "// count is 0 is released when the outermost C entry ends (capiLeave: a ctypes foreign call, an extension module's"] [187 1 "// function, its PyInit), after the result was taken: its map entries dropped (the object is Go's again alone) and its"] [188 1 "// memory freed. A borrowed reference is so valid until the Python code that called C runs again, as CPython's while"] [189 1 "// its owner holds it. Types and the singletons are immortal (never released): their count is CPython's"] [190 1 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_INITIAL_REFCNT, which Include/refcount.h's inline Py_INCREF leaves alone (>= it) and Py_DECREF too"] [191 1 "// (_Py_IsImmortal: >= _Py_IMMORTAL_MINIMUM_REFCNT)."] [193 24 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_INITIAL_REFCNT (64 bits)"] [194 24 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_MINIMUM_REFCNT"] [198 19 "// the proxies whose count was 0 at some point since the last release"] [199 19 "// the C entries in progress (capiEnter, capiLeave)"] [202 1 "// handle is o's PyObject *: its proxy's address (made on the first use: ob_refcnt 0, or immortal for a type; ob_type"] [203 1 "// its type's handle)."] [213 21 "// a C-born object (queue 268): its memory"] [216 27 "// a C type's instance over a built-in base (queue 269): its memory"] [219 2 "// the head of a PyVarObject (Include/object.h): ob_refcnt, ob_type and ob_size, which the limited API's inline"] [220 2 "// Py_SIZE reads (queue 262: PySlice_GetIndicesEx's macro over a list); since queue 269 a type's PyTypeObject and"] [221 2 "// a tuple's, list's, bytes' or float's mirror (capi_mirror.go)"] [228 33 "// a C metaclass's instance (queue 270b): its C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject"] [235 24 "// queue 521: PyModuleObject, md_state read in place"] [239 27 "// queue 568: PyCMethodObject, PyCFunction_GET_SELF and GET_FUNCTION read in place"] [243 13 "// PyStructObject: s_size, s_len, s_codes, s_format, weakreflist (queue 473: _testbuffer's get_nmemb)"] [269 29 "// a type, or a small int (CPython's are immortal: -5 to 256, queue 269)"] [274 35 "// ob_type: its type's handle"] [286 1 "// fromHandle is the object a PyObject * names (nil for NULL or an address that is no proxy)."] [294 23 "// queue 521: a static object of a C type (datetime's utc_timezone)"] [302 1 "// incRef and decRef are Py_IncRef and Py_DecRef on a handle (NULL and the immortal left alone)."] [328 1 "// steal takes C's reference to o's proxy for Python (a new reference C returned: Go holds the object from now on)."] [331 1 "// pin is a reference C's memory keeps for the process (a py_object stored into a ctypes object's memory, or returned"] [332 1 "// by a callback: CPython's object is kept by the ctypes object's _objects, which pyi's handles cannot follow)."] [339 1 "// unpinWith gives the pin of the handle h back once holder is collected (on the library's next call, as cbuf's free)."] [345 1 "// capiEnter and capiLeave bracket a C entry from Python: capiLeave of the outermost releases the proxies C no longer"] [346 1 "// holds and the strings PyArg_ParseTuple handed C. Usage: defer capiLeave(capiEnter())."] [350 3 "// the C-born objects Go collected: their tp_dealloc (queue 268), inside the entry (queue 473: a dealloc that"] [351 3 "// enters C again, ndarray_dealloc's PyBuffer_Release of a view, must not leave the outermost entry and release"] [352 3 "// the handles this entry's caller just made for it)"] [358 1 "// reapAtCollect is py's ExtReap (a collection's rounds, finalize.go; py-breaker-1126): the C-born objects Go collected"] [359 1 "// deallocated now, in an entry of their own (capiEnter's reapDead, capiLeave releasing what they held), not at the world's"] [360 1 "// next entry; nothing inside a C entry (a collection C or its callback started: the outermost entry reaps)."] [387 21 "// Py_AddPendingCall's, when C has returned to Python (py-capi-1122)"] [391 1 "// releaseUnowned releases every proxy of count 0 (outside any C entry)."] [399 2 "// a free runs the library's deferred work first (unpinWith's), which may add to the list: taken before; a"] [400 2 "// mirror released gives its items back, which may release them too (queue 269): until none is left"] [412 14 "// a C-born object's memory is its own: freed by its tp_dealloc once Go collects it (queue 268)"] [415 14 "// so is a C type's instance over a built-in base (queue 269)"] [427 1 "// varProxies are the proxies of the mutable variable-size objects (lists, bytearrays), whose ob_size refreshSizes"] [428 1 "// keeps current."] [431 1 "// varSize is ob_size of the variable-size objects CPython gives one (tuples, lists, bytes, bytearrays) and whether it"] [432 1 "// can change."] [435 37 "// tuples, lists and bytes are mirrors since queue 269"] [439 32 "// ma_used, at ob_size's offset (PyDict_GET_SIZE, queue 270)"] [447 1 "// refreshSizes writes the current ob_size of the mutable proxies (after a native: C reads it inline, and the native"] [448 1 "// may have run Python code that resized the object)."] [461 1 "// liveHandles is the number of proxies (the probe's count of the handles C keeps)."] [464 1 "// isSmallInt is an exact int of -5 to 256 (pyi's are interned as CPython's, which are immortal)."] [474 1 "// goMap is a Python buffer's bytes mapped into the world's address space (queue 261: from_buffer shares a bytearray's,"] [475 1 "// an array's or a memoryview's memory, as CPython's ctypes object points into the exporter's buffer): a slab at a free"] [476 1 "// address of the mappings' region whose bytes are the buffer's own, so C, the ctypes object and Python see each"] [477 1 "// other's writes. The exporter cannot move them while the ctypes object keeps its memoryview (a resize is refused)."] [480 1 "// mapGo maps b; the mapping is removed once the goMap is collected (on the library's next call, as cbuf's free)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[49 36] [51 49] [66 28] [69 30] [73 27] [92 22] [208 25] [212 19] [215 19] [227 30] [261 34] [288 21] [296 23] [308 21] [411 25] [417 23] [436 25] [440 24] [455 28]]} (go/file "world.go" :imports [

